# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VRMPet
#
# Source that IS tracked: CMakeLists.txt, build.sh, REPORT.md, src/, tools/,
# and third_party/wicked_importer/ (that last one is a deliberate byte-for-byte
# copy of the engine's Editor/ModelImporter_GLTF.cpp - see REPORT.md section
# 4.4 - so it must stay in the repository).
#
# Everything else below is generated.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build tree
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# build.sh configures into build/ and copies VRMPet.exe, dxcompiler.dll and the
# compiled shaders into build/run/. All of it is derived: CMakeCache.txt, the
# Ninja files, object files, and every capture the tool produces.
build/
build-*/
cmake-build-*/

# build.sh writes its full transcript here.
build_vrmpet.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CMake
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
CMakeUserPresets.json
cmake_install.cmake
CTestTestfile.cmake
install_manifest.txt
compile_commands.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MSVC / Windows toolchain
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.obj
*.o
*.exe
*.lib
*.exp
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.idb
*.res
*.tlog
*.lastbuildstate
*.log

# Generated Visual Studio project files, for anyone who configures with -G VS.
.vs/
*.sln
*.vcxproj
*.vcxproj.filters
*.vcxproj.user

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Capture output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VRMPet.exe writes these into its output directory, and the tools in tools/
# write the derived images next to them. Named individually rather than with a
# blanket *.png, so a screenshot that is worth keeping can still be committed.
mask_default.png
mask_user.png
mask_nostencil.png
background.png
color.png
engine.log
log.txt
run.log
diff_full.png
diff_head.png
mask_default_head.png
mask_user_head.png
mask_default_over_checker.png
mask_user_over_checker.png
head_composite_vs_truth.png

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
